  "question": {
    "text": "The resultant of two forces $\\mathrm{P~N}$ and $3 \\mathrm{~N}$ is a force of $7 \\mathrm{~N}$. If the direction of $3 \\mathrm{~N}$ force were reversed, the resultant would be $\\sqrt{19} \\mathrm{~N}$. The value of $\\mathrm{P}$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ODBac",
      "text": "\n$5 \\mathrm{~N}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "NFwHO",
      "text": "\n$6 \\mathrm{~N}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "H6yiv",
      "text": "\n$3 \\mathrm{~N}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "4GgGS",
      "text": "\n$4 \\mathrm{~N}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/zSxUTGY5QCK2424Wy8kFzqI5moFKhrWdXKSHmMhrxTQ.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& 7^2=P^2+3^2+2 \\times 3 \\times P \\cos \\theta \\quad \\dots(1)\\\\\n& (\\sqrt{19})^2=P^2+(-3)^2+2 \\times(-3) \\times P \\cos \\theta \\quad \\dots (2)\n\\end{aligned}$\nadding we get\n$68=2 P^2+18 \\Rightarrow P=5$.",
